      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The complete Theorem3.1, Theorem5.1, Corollary5.2, Lemma5.3 and the technical bounded-convergence support lemmas A.2–A.6 are supplied. The standing manifold is a globally hyperbolic spacetime with finitely many connected components and fixed topologically regular compact K; P acts on smooth scalar functions. A(0)=0, range A(lambda) is supported in K, the stated distribution/Sobolev extensions improve total regularity by delta=beta+gamma>0, and A(lambda)E+/- is holomorphic at all relevant Sobolev levels. The full source assumptions (a)–(d) and the stronger (d-prime) alternative are retained literally, without reducing them to the misleading shorthand smoothing perturbation. Established Green-hyperbolic extension theory and analytic Fredholm theory are background; the new smooth/LF inversion, Green identities, parameter continuity and support construction are fully proved here. The dual-kernel comparison3.5 and special integral-kernel corollaries are not counted separately."
      },
